{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   MEMBER ACCOUNT AUTH — the shell every public account screen wears.

   Sign in, register and the verification notice are three screens with one
   frame: warm ground, brand lockup, one white card, and whatever each screen
   wants to put under it. The frame lives here once.

   ── WHY A LAYOUT AND NOT THREE COPIES ──────────────────────────────────────
   It was three copies. The brand lockup, the column and the footer credit were
   repeated in `login.twig`, `register.twig` and `verify-notice.twig`, so the
   copyright line and the logo mark-up existed three times and could disagree.
   They already had: the sign-in said "Member account" over a pitch about
   points while registration said something else entirely, and nothing on any
   screen showed the drift.

   ── NOT `layout/auth.twig`, AND NOT `components/auth.css` ──────────────────
   The admin console, the judges' panel and the organisation sign-in are
   separate trust domains on separate routes, deliberately without a shared
   public entry point (see the design handoff §5). They keep the older
   two-column `.ag-auth` shell. Nothing here may reach them.

   Fill `card` with the card's contents, `below` with anything under it.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% extends "layout/gates.twig" %}

{% block head_styles %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/account-auth.css') }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="ag-acct">
  <div class="ag-acct__col">

    <a class="ag-acct__brand" href="/" aria-label="Africa GATES — home">
      <span class="ag-acct__mark" aria-hidden="true">G</span>
      <span class="ag-acct__word">Africa <span>GATES</span></span>
    </a>

    <div class="ag-acct__card">
      {% block card %}{% endblock %}
    </div>

    {% block below %}{% endblock %}

    <p class="ag-acct__credit">© {{ "now"|date("Y") }} Africa GATES · An Afrovanguard initiative</p>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
